Package: underwood
Version: 2.6.7
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), xterm, fonts-dejavu-core, hunspell, hunspell-es, xclip, hunspell-en-us
Recommends: libreoffice-writer
Maintainer: Silvestre Parbut
Homepage: https://github.com/SilvestreParbut/Underwood
Description: A word processor for the terminal.
 Underwood is a minimalist word processor for the terminal, designed for creative writing—novels, short stories, essays, and screenplays
 It includes text formatting (bold, italics, underlining), three levels of headings with a chapter map, a spell checker (using Hunspell), search and replace, and export options for RTF, TXT, DOCX, and PDF
 It supports mouse input, but can also be operated entirely via the keyboard: use Shift+arrow keys for selection, and the F9 key to access menus
